    skos:editorialNote "Question: source not stated, from the 2021-22 Data Capture Format."@en ;
    dct:references "DCF item 2.27" ;
    dct:provenance "Shared 2018-19 to 2021-22 as smallint, described as “ICT Lab available in school”"@en ;
    dct:isVersionOf udise:series.facility_data.ict_lab ;
    skos:altLabel "ict_lab_yn"@en ;
    skos:historyNote "{\"at\": \"2021-22 to 2022-23\", \"action\": \"RENAME\", \"from\": \"ict_lab\", \"to\": \"ict_lab_yn\", \"basis\": \"DCF item 2.27 'Is ICT Lab available in the school?' is word for word identical in 2021-22 and 2022-23. The question did not move. The Ministry's release description did: it narrows the shared column to 'ICT Lab available in school under Samagra Siksha', a restriction the form does not carry\", \"similarity\": null, \"confidence\": \"confirmed\", \"how\": \"form\"}"@en ;
    skos:note "undocumented-code-9: Nine released columns hold a code 9 that the Data Capture Format never defines. The form offers 1-Yes and 2-No. The file carries a third value, and for two columns a 0 as well. No published document says what either means."@en ;
    skos:note "union-artefact: A union of eight yearly files keeps every column any year ever had. These four ended at 2021-22. UDISE dropped them at the SDMIS break. The columns remain and read NULL for every later row."@en .

