    skos:note "type-code-as-binary: A column that looks like a yes/no carries more codes than yes and no. boundary_wall has eight types. electricity_availability, solar_panel and rain_water_harvesting each carry a third code, 'yes but not functional'. Read `= 1` as the affirmative and every other code silently becomes a negative. Read this column's own code list, shown above, before averaging anything."@en .

